## Remediation

The vulnerability arises from the improper handling of untrusted user input when using the `eval` function, `Function` constructor, `setTimeout`, or `setInterval` methods in JavaScript. Evaluating user input in this manner can lead to arbitrary code execution, allowing an attacker to run malicious code within the application. This poses a severe security risk, enabling various attacks like Remote Code Execution (RCE), Cross-Site Scripting (XSS), and data tampering.

