SQL Injection is a critical vulnerability that allows an attacker to execute malicious SQL statements by injecting malicious input into application queries. This can lead to unauthorized data access, data manipulation, and in some cases, complete system compromise. SQL Injection attacks are often severe due to the sensitive nature of data stored in databases and the elevated privileges with which the database operates.

To fix this issue, user input should never be concatenated directly into SQL queries. Instead, use parameterized queries or an object-relational mapping (ORM) library's built-in data binding mechanisms. Sequelize provides methods like `replace` and `escape` to safely construct queries with user input.

