XML External Entity (XXE) Processing vulnerabilities occur when an XML parser is instructed to resolve external entities, which can lead to disclosing sensitive data, remote code execution, or denial of service attacks. This vulnerability arises when user-controlled data is passed to an XML parser without proper sanitization or validation.

To fix this issue, you should disable the ability to resolve external entities in the XML parser configuration. Additionally, validate and sanitize any user input that is passed to the XML parser to prevent injection of malicious content.

#### Code examples

```javascript
// VULNERABLE CODE - User input is passed directly to the XML parser
const libxmljs = require("libxmljs");
const parser = new libxmljs.SaxParser();
const userInput = req.query.input;
parser.parseString(userInput, (err, result) => {
  // ...
});
```

```javascript
// SECURE CODE - Disable external entity resolution and sanitize user input
const libxmljs = require("libxmljs");
