The default session middleware settings in Express.js do not set an expiration date for persistent cookies, which can lead to session hijacking and other attacks. Persistent cookies without an expiration date never expire, allowing an attacker to potentially gain unauthorized access to a user's session indefinitely.

To fix this issue, you should set the `expires` option when configuring the session middleware. This option specifies the maximum age of the session cookie in milliseconds. After this time, the cookie will become invalid, and the user will be logged out.

