The default session cookie name used by popular Node.js session management libraries like `cookie-session` and `express-session` is well-known and can be used by attackers to fingerprint the server and potentially target attacks more effectively. Using a non-default, unique session cookie name can help mitigate this risk.

To fix this issue, you should configure the session management library to use a custom, unique session cookie name. This can typically be done by passing an options object with the `name` property set to the desired cookie name.

